# ==============================================================================
# TIO ValidityCandidate Extension
# ==============================================================================
#
# Purpose:
#   This file extends TM Forum Intent Ontology (TIO) v3.6.0 with semantic
#   classification for entities that can have validity assigned to them.
#
# Rationale:
#   TIO 3.6.0 iv:sameValidityAs property can only point to Intent OR Expectation.
#   Currently this requires complex SPARQL with multiple FILTER NOT EXISTS
#   patterns to validate the union of these two types:
#
#   FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?value a ?t . ?t rdfs:subClassOf* icm:Intent . }
#   FILTER NOT EXISTS { ?value a ?t . ?t rdfs:subClassOf* icm:Expectation . }
#
#   This extension provides a single mixin class that enables:
#   - Simple sh:class validation or single FILTER NOT EXISTS
#   - Automatic inheritance via rdfs:subClassOf*
#   - Clear semantic documentation of what can have validity
#
# Design:
#   These extensions are separated from the TIO baseline to:
#   - Keep TIO 3.6.0 ontology files pristine and unchanged
#   - Enable clean merging of future TIO updates
#   - Simplify proposing these additions upstream to TM Forum
#
# Compatibility:
#   - Backward compatible: All existing valid intents remain valid
#   - Forward compatible: New Intent/Expectation subclasses automatically inherit
#   - Zero breaking changes to TIO 3.6.0 semantics
#
# ==============================================================================

@prefix iv:   <http://tio.models.tmforum.org/tio/v3.6.0/IntentValidityOntology/> .
@prefix icm:  <http://tio.models.tmforum.org/tio/v3.6.0/IntentCommonModel/> .
@prefix rdf:  <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#> .
@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix xsd:  <http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#> .

# ==============================================================================
# SECTION 1: Core Class Definition
# ==============================================================================
#
# The iv:ValidityCandidate mixin class identifies entities that can have
# validity assigned to them. Only Intents and Expectations can have validity -
# other IntentElement subclasses like Target cannot.
#
# ==============================================================================

iv:ValidityCandidate
  rdfs:label "Validity Candidate Class"@en ;
  rdfs:comment """Things that can have validity assigned to them.

  Only Intents and Expectations can have validity - other IntentElement
  subclasses like Target cannot. This mixin class enables:
  - Simple range constraints for iv:sameValidityAs
  - Single FILTER NOT EXISTS pattern instead of multiple unions
  - Clear semantic documentation of validity semantics

  SHACL validation uses rdfs:subClassOf* to find all ValidityCandidate instances."""@en ;
  rdf:type rdfs:Class
.

# ==============================================================================
# SECTION 2: Intent Common Model Extensions
# ==============================================================================
#
# Mark Intent and Expectation as ValidityCandidate.
# Note: Expectation subclasses (PropertyExpectation, DeliveryExpectation,
# ReportingExpectation) inherit ValidityCandidate via rdfs:subClassOf*.
#
# ==============================================================================

icm:Intent
  rdfs:subClassOf iv:ValidityCandidate .

icm:Expectation
  rdfs:subClassOf iv:ValidityCandidate .

# ==============================================================================
# SECTION 3: Vocabulary Extension
# ==============================================================================
#
# Adds extension term to iv:Vocabulary so it is recognized by vocabulary
# validation constraints.
#
# ==============================================================================

iv:Vocabulary
  rdfs:member iv:ValidityCandidate .

# ==============================================================================
# End of ValidityCandidateExtension.ttl
# ==============================================================================
